          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A network diagram consists of vertices joined by edges. Assume no loops (no edge from a vertex to itself).",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q27-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Suppose the network has 15 vertices. For each pair of distinct vertices, an edge may be absent, or it may be present. How many possible networks can be formed?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2^{105}$ networks.\n\nThere are $\\binom{15}{2}=105$ pairs, with two independent choices for each pair.",
          "worked": "The number of unordered pairs of vertices is $\\binom{15}{2}=105$. Each pair has two states: an edge is absent or present. By the multiplication principle,\n$$N=2^{105}.$$\nThere are $2^{105}$ networks.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q27-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "In a directed network, each pair of distinct vertices $A$, $B$, an edge may be absent, or it may be directed $A\\to B$, directed $B\\to A$, or present both ways. How many directed networks can be formed on 15 vertices?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4^{105}$ directed networks.\n\nEach of the 105 unordered pairs has four independent edge states.",
          "worked": "There are $\\binom{15}{2}=105$ unordered pairs. For each pair there are four states: neither direction, $A\\to B$ only, $B\\to A$ only, or both directions. By the multiplication principle,\n$$N=4^{105}.$$\nThere are $4^{105}$ directed networks.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
